    <bpmn:process id="W_W1839" name="W1839. Private Label Customer Quality Complaint Investigation &amp; Corrective Action" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer complaint received for private label product quality issue
Frequency: ~50–100 quality complaints/month across private label portfolio (~0.5% of transactions involving private label items)
Volume: Range: packaging defects, product performance failure, safety concerns, labeling errors
Owner: Quality Assurance Manager
Participants: QA Manager, Store Manager (complaint receipt), Category Manager, Buyer, Factory
Source: workflow W1839 — Private Label Customer Quality Complaint Investigation &amp; Corrective Action</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1839_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1839_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1839_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1839_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1839_Lane2" name="QA Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1839_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1839_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1839_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1839_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1839_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1839_Start4" name="Customer complaint received for private label product quality issue">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1839_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1839_Task5" name="Customer reports quality issue at store or through customer service: (a) Store…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer reports quality issue at store or through customer service: (a) Store Manager / CSR logs complaint in system with: product (SKU), lot/batch number (if visible), complaint type (safety, performance, cosmetic, packaging), description, customer contact, (b) if safety concern (e.g., power tool malfunction causing injury): Store Manager immediately removes remaining units from shelf and quarantines; QA Manager notified within 2 hours
Responsible (R): Store Manager / CSR
Accountable (A): QA Manager
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1839_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1839_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1839_Task6" name="Safety complaint">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: QA Manager triages complaint: (a) Safety complaint: highest priority — immediate investigation within 24 hours; if confirmed safety risk: escalate to product recall evaluation per W1841, (b) Performance complaint: standard priority — investigate within 5 business days, (c) Cosmetic/packaging complaint: low priority — log for trend analysis; batch for quarterly factory communication
Responsible (R): QA Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1839_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1839_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1839_Task7" name="QA Manager investigates root cause: (a) review complaint details: batch number…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: QA Manager investigates root cause: (a) review complaint details: batch number, manufacturing date, store, customer usage description, (b) compare to reference sample retained from W1832: is the defective unit within specification or a clear outlier? (c) review factory incoming inspection records for the batch: was the batch flagged at receipt? (d) if systemic: review all incoming quality data from same factory for trending defect patterns, (e) if isolated: document as one-off and monitor for recurrence, (f) request factory investigation for performance and safety complaints: factory must respond within 10 business days with root cause analysis and corrective action plan
Responsible (R): QA Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1839_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1839_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1839_Task8" name="Resolution and corrective action: (a) customer resolution: return/exchange per…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Resolution and corrective action: (a) customer resolution: return/exchange per W12 (returns), additional compensation if safety-related, (b) factory corrective action: QA Manager evaluates factory response; if acceptable: track implementation per W1838 corrective action process; if inadequate: escalate to Buyer for supplier intervention, (c) if systemic quality issue confirmed: Buyer and Category Manager decide — (i) continue with factory corrective action, (ii) halt future orders pending quality verification, (iii) initiate supplier transition per W1837, (d) store-level actions: if specific batch affected, issue batch hold notice to all stores carrying the SKU
Responsible (R): QA Manager / Buyer
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1839_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1839_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1839_Task9" name="Monthly: QA Manager compiles private label quality dashboard: (a) complaint…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly: QA Manager compiles private label quality dashboard: (a) complaint rate by SKU, category, and factory, (b) complaint resolution time vs. SLA, (c) top 10 SKUs by complaint volume, (d) factory corrective action closure rate, (e) trending: complaint rate improvement or deterioration by factory
Responsible (R): QA Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1839_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1839_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1839_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1839_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1839_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-365 (ensure controlled execution — Private Label Quality Assurance &amp; Compliance (PA-41.2).) | - operational: Quality Assurance Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Quality Assurance Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1839_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1839_Annotation11" targetRef="W1839_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
