    <bpmn:process id="W_W1841" name="W1841. Private Label Product Recall &amp; Safety Notification" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Confirmed safety defect in private label product; regulatory recall order; factory notification of production defect affecting shipped units
Frequency: Rare — estimated 1–2 recall events/year for private label portfolio
Volume: Affects specific SKU(s), batch(es), and potentially all units across 200 stores
Owner: VP Merchandising
Participants: VP Merchandising, QA Manager, Category Manager, Store Operations, Legal Counsel, Customer Service, CMO
Source: workflow W1841 — Private Label Product Recall &amp; Safety Notification</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1841_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1841_Lane1" name="QA Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1841_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1841_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1841_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1841_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1841_Lane2" name="Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1841_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1841_Lane3" name="Customer Service">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1841_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1841_Lane4" name="Buyer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1841_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1841_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1841_Start6" name="Confirmed safety defect in private label product; regulatory recall order; factory…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1841_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1841_Task7" name="Recall trigger: (a) QA Manager confirms safety defect through investigation per…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Recall trigger: (a) QA Manager confirms safety defect through investigation per W1839 (customer complaint), incoming inspection finding, or factory notification, (b) Legal Counsel assesses regulatory obligation: is a mandatory recall required by DTI, FDA, or DENR? (c) VP Merchandising convenes recall decision meeting within 24 hours of confirmed safety defect
Responsible (R): QA Manager / VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1841_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1841_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1841_Task8" name="Recall scope definition: (a) QA Manager identifies affected batch(es) using lot…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Recall scope definition: (a) QA Manager identifies affected batch(es) using lot tracking data: which factories, which production dates, which DCs received, which stores received, (b) Category Manager quantifies affected units: on shelves, in backrooms, in transit, at DCs, (c) VP Merchandising approves recall scope: full recall (all units) or targeted recall (specific batches only)
Responsible (R): QA Manager / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4–8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1841_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1841_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1841_Task9" name="Recall execution: (a) Store Operations issues immediate store notification…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Recall execution: (a) Store Operations issues immediate store notification: remove affected SKU(s) from shelves and quarantine in backroom, (b) DC operations quarantine any affected units at DCs, (c) customer service contact center: prepare customer communication script, (d) CMO prepares public recall notice (if required): press release, social media, website notice, in-store signage, (e) ecommerce: remove affected SKU from online catalog immediately, (f) legal counsel files mandatory recall notice with DTI/FDA if required
Responsible (R): Store Operations / CMO / Legal
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1841_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1841_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1841_Task10" name="Customer notification and remedy: (a) for loyalty members who purchased…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Customer notification and remedy: (a) for loyalty members who purchased affected product: system generates customer list; customer service contacts customers proactively, (b) remedy: full refund, replacement with national brand equivalent, or store credit — per Category Manager decision, (c) process returns per W12 (returns workflow), (d) for trade accounts: Account Manager contacts trade customers directly
Responsible (R): Customer Service / Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Ongoing for recall duration</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1841_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1841_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1841_Task11" name="Factory accountability: (a) Buyer notifies factory of recall; provides defect…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Factory accountability: (a) Buyer notifies factory of recall; provides defect details and batch information, (b) factory conducts root cause analysis (mandatory), (c) QA Manager evaluates factory corrective action, (d) Buyer negotiates cost recovery: reimbursement for recalled units, refund processing costs, customer compensation costs, (e) if factory cooperation inadequate: Category Manager initiates supplier transition per W1837
Responsible (R): Buyer / QA Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1841_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1841_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1841_Task12" name="Post-recall review: (a) QA Manager documents lessons learned: root cause…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Post-recall review: (a) QA Manager documents lessons learned: root cause, detection timing, recall effectiveness, (b) update factory risk assessment and audit frequency, (c) update product specification if design change warranted, (d) VP Merchandising reports to CEO on recall cost, customer impact, and preventive measures
Responsible (R): QA Manager / VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1841_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1841_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1841_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1841_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1841_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-365 (ensure controlled execution — Private Label Quality Assurance &amp; Compliance (PA-41.2).) | - operational: VP Merchandising review and approval gate
Owner: VP Merchandising</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1841_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1841_Annotation14" targetRef="W1841_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
