    <bpmn:process id="W_W1842" name="W1842. Private Label Shelf-Life Monitoring &amp; Near-Expiry Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly shelf-life review; near-expiry alert from inventory system
Frequency: Monthly review for shelf-life managed private label products
Volume: ~200–400 SKUs with shelf life (adhesives, sealants, paint accessories, chemicals, cleaning products)
Owner: Merchandise Planner
Participants: Merchandise Planner, Category Manager, Store Operations Coordinator
Source: workflow W1842 — Private Label Shelf-Life Monitoring &amp; Near-Expiry Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1842_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1842_Lane1" name="Merchandise Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1842_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1842_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1842_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1842_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1842_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1842_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1842_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1842_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1842_Start4" name="Monthly shelf-life review; near-expiry alert from inventory system">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1842_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1842_Task5" name="Monthly: Merchandise Planner generates shelf-life aging report for private…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly: Merchandise Planner generates shelf-life aging report for private label products: (a) SKUs with remaining shelf life &lt; 6 months flagged amber, (b) SKUs with remaining shelf life &lt; 3 months flagged red, (c) SKUs past expiry date flagged critical
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1842_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1842_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1842_Task6" name="For amber-flagged SKUs (6 months remaining): (a) Category Manager evaluates: is…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: For amber-flagged SKUs (6 months remaining): (a) Category Manager evaluates: is current sell-through rate sufficient to sell through before expiry? (b) if yes: no action, monitor next month, (c) if sell-through too slow: implement promotional pricing per W93 (markdown) to accelerate movement, (d) prioritize movement at stores with oldest inventory (FEFO compliance)
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1842_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1842_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1842_Task7" name="For red-flagged SKUs (3 months remaining): (a) Category Manager authorizes…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: For red-flagged SKUs (3 months remaining): (a) Category Manager authorizes aggressive markdown (25–40%), (b) offer to trade accounts at bulk discount, (c) move remaining inventory to higher-traffic stores if distribution is uneven
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1842_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1842_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1842_Task8" name="For critical-flagged SKUs (past expiry): (a) Merchandise Planner generates…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: For critical-flagged SKUs (past expiry): (a) Merchandise Planner generates write-off request per W220 (SLOB provisioning), (b) Store Operations coordinates removal and disposal (environmentally compliant disposal for chemical products per DENR requirements), (c) system adjusts inventory and posts write-off to GL
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner / Store Operations
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: Per W220</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1842_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1842_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1842_Task9" name="Quarterly: Category Manager reviews shelf-life write-off trends: (a) by product…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly: Category Manager reviews shelf-life write-off trends: (a) by product category and factory, (b) identify SKUs with recurring shelf-life issues for potential discontinuation, (c) adjust order quantities and safety stock for shelf-life managed SKUs to reduce future waste
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 hour/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1842_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1842_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1842_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1842_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1842_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-365 (ensure controlled execution — Private Label Quality Assurance &amp; Compliance (PA-41.2).) | - operational: Merchandise Planner review and approval gate
Owner: Merchandise Planner</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1842_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1842_Annotation11" targetRef="W1842_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1842_Flow13" sourceRef="W1842_Start4" targetRef="W1842_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1842_Flow14" sourceRef="W1842_Task5" targetRef="W1842_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1842_Flow15" sourceRef="W1842_Task6" targetRef="W1842_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1842_Flow16" sourceRef="W1842_Task7" targetRef="W1842_Task8" />
